The shop holds only 20 sets, but they
hold 35% of its value at cost, because each set is
heavy and costly.

**Question.** The antique jhumka (EAR-0001) costs
₹1,16,640 a pair, and the shop has
8 pairs. What are they worth at
cost?

::: {.callout-tip collapse="true"}
## Answer

8 × ₹1,16,640 =
₹9,33,120, which the app writes
as ₹9.33 L.
:::

::: {.remember}
- One design is one product, with its own SKU.
- Earrings are counted in pairs, sets as one and the rest in pieces, and
  these are never added together.
- Stock value is stock on hand times cost (or list price). It always says
  which, and from when.
:::
